            {
              "about": "Pin and Turn",
              "decided": "plugins/pin and plugins/turn go once rn holds their parts. The branch turn-held keeps the eight Turn commits no branch held, rn takes each where its design keeps what it fixes, then the branch goes",
              "by": "reasoning"
            },
            {
              "about": "Lane's old part folders",
              "decided": "Lane's guard stops reading prompts/ and core/roles/ in the change that removes Pin and Turn, as their parts lie there until then",
              "by": "reasoning"
            },
            {
              "about": "A null start value",
              "decided": "a run lane whose value is null lets no command through, and a run_step command the adapter gives counts as allowed, so the generator gets run_only",
              "by": "reasoning"
            },
            {
              "about": "A file a role must not read",
              "decided": "Lane gains a lane that stops a read of the files it names, and the planner and generator get it for the design tree, as no role reads the tree",
              "by": "reasoning"
            },
            {
              "about": "Permission for tree.py",
              "decided": "the skill names tree.py in allowed-tools, and the prose check reads no front matter, as a prompt per call costs the user time",
              "by": "reasoning"
            },
            {
              "about": "Picking up a run on another branch",
              "decided": "/rn:up alone finds the runs on rn's work branches and picks up the one the user means, asking only where more than one waits",
              "by": "reasoning"
            },
            {
              "about": "The code made before",
              "decided": "rn's code and tests made before go whole, and the improved code best practice makes rn anew, as no one can tell where code made without it falls short",
